{{define "title"}}Your Chronos password appeared in a data breach{{end}}
{{define "content"}}
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;">Hello{{if .Name}} {{.Name}}{{end}},</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;">The password on your Chronos account appears in a public breach
  corpus{{if .Source}} ({{.Source}}){{end}}. We found this while you signed in on
  <strong>{{datetime .OccurredAt}}</strong>.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 14px;">Chronos was not breached. The password itself is known to attackers,
  wherever you first used it, and anyone with the list can try it here.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 20px;">We have not locked you out — you can still sign in, and your session is
  restricted to your profile and credentials until the password is replaced.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 20px;">
  <a href="{{url "/settings/security"}}" style="display:inline-block;background:#b42318;color:#ffffff;text-decoration:none;padding:11px 20px;border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:500;">Change your password</a>
</p>
<p style="margin:0;color:#6b7280;font-size:13px;">If you use this password anywhere else, change it there too.</p>
{{end}}
